o:91,121` and `internal/scheduler/parser.go:30`) is **never used by the server**. The only importers of `github.com/usememos/memos/internal/scheduler` are its own tests (`internal/scheduler/example_test.go:10`, `internal/scheduler/integration_test.go:13`), and the code graph returns a certified zero for callers of `scheduler.New`. The s3presign runner rolls its own ticker instead.\n- **`server/runner/memopayload`** — has a `Runner` with `RunOnce` (`server/runner/memopayload/runner.go:27`) that rebuilds all memo payloads, but **nothing constructs it**: callers of `memopayload.NewRunner` and `memopayload.Runner.RunOnce` are a certified zero, and `[ArchMap query]` shows exactly one edge — `NewRunner`'s own return type. Only its package-level helper `RebuildMemoPayload` is live, called inline from request handlers (`server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go:108,447`). So the batch runner is effectively dead scheduling capacity.","iteration":17,"turn":1,"type":"assistant"}
